// offline-voice-gaps-run.bml — the gap register: one native door observes every gap on the way to 100% offline voice and
// says, per gap, closed, open or unread, with the numbers it read and the file it read them from.
//
//   ./fkwu observe/offline-voice-gaps-run.bml </dev/null
//
// The gaps are data, learn/offline-voice-gaps.jsonl (id, title, kind, source, the reading rule, the goal line served);
// the readers, one per shape, live in form-stdlib/bml/offline-voice-gaps.bml. It reads the ledgers other doors write
// (receipts/local-flow-review.jsonl, native-turn-ledger, alignment-ledger, query-coverage-ledger, local-run-ledger,
// session-rent-ledger, remote-guide-ledger, lora-promotion-ledger, draft-readings-ledger, the walk checkout's
// .hearth/walk-retry.jsonl and receipts/native-training-plan.md) and never writes them. No model opens, no network.
// Prints one `[offline-voice-gaps] <id>: <verdict> — <title>; <observation> (<kind> <source>; serves: <goal>)` line per
// gap and a summary line (the counts), appends one row (at_unix_ms, counts, per-gap verdicts) to
// receipts/offline-voice-gap-register.jsonl, and answers the summary line. Exit 0 when it observed; a missing or empty
// gaps file is refused by name (exit non-zero). docs/offline-voice-gaps.md explains the register.
// stdin, optional, one JSON line: gaps (the gaps file, default learn/offline-voice-gaps.jsonl), root (a directory the
// sources resolve under, for a band), walk (the walk checkout, in place of the one the day-turn plist names; "" is none),
// register (the register path, default receipts/offline-voice-gap-register.jsonl).
// preflight-exec: forbidden
import form-stdlib/bml/offline-voice-gaps.bml;
section [form.bml] {
 ovg-run(ovg-opts());
}
